1
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,097
Sniper Island Oh, the
wind carries my name.

2
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,440
From Sniper Island far away.

3
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,517
When I take aim, it's straight and true.

4
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,200
Blue, blue, la, la, blue.

5
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:36,477
Whether you're a man or a man, go on.

6
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,140
I will put your heart in my sights.

7
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:49,420
No one knows what secrets
hide behind this past edging.

8
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:54,417
Blue, blue, blue, the la, la, la.

9
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,140
There is no escape?

10
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,317
Snipers, sniper, sniper.

11
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,740
Sniper, he hates King, it's true.

12
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,977
The ring carries my name.

13
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:19,420
From Sniper Island far away.

14
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,920
What the hell is he doing over there?

15
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,520
Come on, just humor the poor guy.

16
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,637
He has too much pride to
show his face to the crew,

17
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:38,537
but he still wants to rescue his friend.

18
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:41,000
No one knows what secret I'd be.

19
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:44,140
Well, long as he stops singing, I guess.

20
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,180
Hey, get over here!

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:47,680
Oh, sure.

22
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:57,420
Okay, let's start the meeting
for Operation Rescue Robin.

23
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,937
We've never met before.

24
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,397
Don't you two have any questions about me?

25
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:04,720
So, the car you were
in was car number six.

26
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,057
That means that we've got five more left.

27
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:09,380
You know, like, where's Sniper Island?

28
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,637
But we don't know which
one of those Robin is in.

29
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,920
The answer is, it's in your heart.

30
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:17,320
And by the way, are you strong?

31
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:18,850
Are you kidding?

32
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:20,120
I'm super strong.

33
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:22,437
Even stronger than usual this week.

34
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:25,717
Remember, the point is to rescue
Robin, not beat the enemy.

35
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,000
At least in theory.

36
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:30,377
We're up against a lot of
Marines in a narrow space,

37
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,657
so we gotta make sure
we don't get surrounded.

38
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:37,564
We should avoid as many fights as we can
and whittle down the main force in turns.

39
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,640
Here we go. Listen up.

40
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,060
Okay, now I'm ready for battle.

41
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:48,150
Huh?

42
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:49,063
What's going on?

43
00:02:49,146 --> 00:02:51,017
Don't you play innocent
with me, immoral girl!

44
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:54,617
Have you no shame changing your
clothes out here in front of everyone?

45
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,680
Shame is overrated.

46
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,857
What was I supposed to do?

47
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:01,528
The train only has one car.

48
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,980
Cover up your legs!

49
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,437
Cover up your stomach!

50
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,657
That goes for you two square-hand sisters!

51
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:09,034
People like you are corrupting society!

52
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:12,180
Whatever, you're just too shy. Shy boy.

53
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:13,810
Why you?

54
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:17,780
Stupid black shorts with
their stupid tiny pockets.

55
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,040
Come on!

56
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,320
Get in there!

57
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,617
Don't put meat in your pants, you idiot!

58
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:27,597
I'm starting to think you
might actually pull this off.

59
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,057
You certainly seem riled
up, if nothing else.

60
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,100
You bet we are!

61
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,517
Those jerks got away with Robin last time,

62
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,437
but now that I know what's going
on, they don't stand a chance!

63
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,677
I hope you're right, because if
you get stuck in something again,

64
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,037
you're going to have hell to pay you.

65
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:46,437
Nah don't worry I got a reason to
beat them this time around right?

66
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:49,017
Hey did you Change your weapon?

67
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:55,117
Nami oh no it's pretty much the same
one as before Usopp just improved it

68
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:00,017
with some dials after we got back from
Skypea this is The perfect climate act?

69
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,937
I see so that's his right?

70
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:04,460
It's Usopp's

71
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,720
Last work

72
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,880
Don't get all sad now!

73
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,620
You ready?

74
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,160
Let's do this.

75
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,420
An intruder?

76
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:29,757
Uh, yes, sir.

77
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,016
That's what I heard.

78
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:35,307
It's not feasible to board the
Puffing Tom while it's running.

79
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,017
If there really is an intruder,

80
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:40,394
that means we let him sneak
on board before we departed.

81
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:41,834
What an embarrassment.

82
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,940
I agree, sir.

83
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,080
It's inexcusable.

84
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:49,257
But if you can't get on while the train
is moving, you can't get off either.

85
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:53,477
That means the intruder, as well as the
missing prisoners, are still here somewhere.

86
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,120
You just have to find them. Yes, sir.

87
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:17,972
Captain T-Bone, I don't think there's
any room for someone to hide in here.

88
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,100
Good evening!

89
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,360
It's them!

90
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,232
They were right outside!

91
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:32,877
We found three suspicious men,
including the criminals in Car 7!

92
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,820
Corner and capture them!

93
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,620
Ever use a hammer before?

94
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,880
You sure do suck. Shut up!

95
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:42,757
There's no point in resisting.

96
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:44,340
Open the door already!

97
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,360
They're gonna break through! I know.

98
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,580
This way!

99
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,817
They found the intruder in car seven.

100
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:53,900
The criminals do?

101
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,416
Yeah, let the guys in car three know.

102
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,617
That Franky guy's in a lot of trouble.

103
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:00,524
Move in and capture them alive!

104
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,780
Move it! Stand back!

105
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,150
Whoa!

106
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:07,197
They're shooting at us!

107
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,280
Then hurry it up!

108
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:10,187
A little help would be nice!

109
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,500
Don't shoot blindly!

110
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:17,525
We don't want these guys dead!

111
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:19,270
You're right.

112
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:22,105
What do we do, Captain T-Bone?

113
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:24,440
Allow me to handle this.

114
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,340
I hate crooked men and crooked swordplay.

115
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,920
Here comes my right-angle flash!

116
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:40,020
Bonsoir!

117
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,360
They're gone!

118
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,240
The roof!

119
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:10,930
Go!

120
00:07:11,013 --> 00:07:12,862
They're at the end of the train!

121
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,140
Now, hurry!

122
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:19,920
Oh, no!

123
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,877
Everyone get back to the
front cars right now.

124
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,257
This is a trap!

125
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:26,980
What are you talking about?

126
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:29,437
Quick retreat.

127
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,757
They tricked us. huh.

128
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:33,177
We can't go back anymore.

129
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,297
The door's blocked.

130
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:35,220
No way.

131
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,580
The cars are detached.

132
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:41,370
Whoa!

133
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:44,620
Damn it! That's cheating!

134
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:46,580
You'll pay for this!

135
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:50,680
I was too late.

136
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,980
Have a safe trip, gentlemen!

137
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,500
Say hello to the Sea Kings for me!

138
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:56,880
Fare thee well!

139
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,280
That's two cars down.

140
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:04,597
Should cut the small fries
down by about 50 or so.

141
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:06,957
But aren't Luffy and the others
coming on the same railway?

142
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:09,737
What happens when the
cars run into each other?

143
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:11,879
Eh, they'll come up with something.

144
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:14,340
You arrogant thugs!

145
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:17,147
I'm gonna tear this door
down in you with it!

146
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,740
Oh, going for a swim?

147
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:26,400
All right.

148
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:28,500
Five to go.

149
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,400
You bastard!

150
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:32,237
You're gonna suffer for that one!

151
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,300
What will poor Captain T-Bone do?

152
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:36,557
Hey, report this to CP9!

153
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,200
Great, more of these guys.

154
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,440
And Freight has for T!

155
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,420
Sniper King!

156
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,300
Gunpowder Stark!

157
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,440
Strong right!

158
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,840
Heavyweight shot, fire!

159
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:07,630
Agh!

160
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:08,720
They hit him!

161
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:16,700
That hurt.

162
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,720
Keep shooting!

163
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:29,220
Why isn't the gun working on him?

164
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,940
Whoa, that was crazy.

165
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:44,394
What the hell are you?

166
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,090
Huh?

167
00:09:46,173 --> 00:09:48,620
Oh, guess I forgot to
tell you. I'm a cyborg.

168
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,680
Those are real? Yep.

169
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:53,982
I got steel and weapons
built right into my body.

170
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,777
Still kind of hurts if I get shot,
and I might bleed a little too.

171
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,280
But no big deal.

172
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:03,497
Just when you think you've seen
it all, the world's a crazy place.

173
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:04,410
Awesome!

174
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:07,530
Oh...

175
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:11,780
What in the hell was that for? Huh?

176
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,097
You can deflect bullets, but needles hurt?

177
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:17,097
For one, I'm not your science
experiment, so stop poking me!

178
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:21,437
And for two, just so you know, my back
isn't the same as my front, get it?

179
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:25,497
I had to do the operation on myself,
so I couldn't reach around behind me.

180
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:28,286
In other words, only the
front side is cyborg.

181
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,297
While I'm at it, let me tell
you another little secret.

182
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,980
My belly's always cold.

183
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,299
Can you guess why?

184
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,600
How would I know?

185
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,737
It's because I got my own personal
fridge in there to keep my cola cold.

186
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:41,080
Wow, that's handy.

187
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:43,771
Man, that's got to be great in the summer.

188
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:47,557
Okay, the cola thing is really neat,
but we don't have time for this.

189
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,993
We've got to get moving to the next car.

190
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,632
This one is number four.

191
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:06,170
I'm Wanze!

192
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,380
Here I come!

193
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,300
What's up, you guys? Are you hungry?

194
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,270
You look hungry.

195
00:11:24,353 --> 00:11:25,183
How about some ramen?

196
00:11:25,266 --> 00:11:26,657
I'm the head steward of this train,

197
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:29,017
so I can cook anything you
fellas would like to eat.

198
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:32,697
Okay, ramen it is, but before I
start, a little trivia for you.

199
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:34,839
My nose hairs are shaped like this.

200
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:38,737
They crisscross inside, so they
look just like fishnet stockings.

201
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,420
This is very important.

202
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,397
First, I grab the flour.

203
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,480
Ant feet in...

204
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,160
No, no, take this!

205
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:56,910
Done!

206
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:58,640
Here... Oh, no!

207
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:02,040
Okay, that was a waste of time.

208
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:05,520
Listen, we've got someone
waiting on us, Wanze.

209
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:08,557
You'll have to enjoy that
nose ramen on your own.

210
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,240
Not so fast!

211
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:15,220
You'll have to defeat me first!

212
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,480
You think you can stop us?

213
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:23,740
I know I can!

214
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,860
This is an important escort mission,

215
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:32,020
so they've got an important guy
like me to keep the train safe!

216
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:35,537
If you want to rescue
that friend of yours,

217
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:38,444
then first you'll have
to defeat my Ramen Kenpo!

218
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:41,580
Ramen Kenpo?

219
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,774
I mean, keep gambling!

220
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:47,440
That little turd is making fun of me!

221
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:50,137
I know he's annoying, but
you gotta keep your cool!

222
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,137
How'd you like my idiot imitation?

223
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,808
Was it dumb enough for you?

224
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,917
Don't let him get to you.

225
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,120
Go, go, go, go, go!

226
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:00,333
This dude got ants in his pants or what?

227
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,021
I swear that I crazed him
with one of those shots.

228
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,697
But he doesn't even care.

229
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:12,956
He even looks happy.

230
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,877
I thought my heart was going
to leap out of my chest.

231
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,037
How was I supposed to know?

232
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:19,257
You made that same stupid
face for everything.

233
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:22,620
I'll take this guy down.
Just watch. Hold on.

234
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:25,397
You can't let this clown
get under your skin.

235
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:28,717
We got more important things to
do than sit here and play games.

236
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,506
You stay back and I'll
make quick work of him.

237
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,937
I don't know what your deal is?

238
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:38,667
But if you were a real chef, you'd conduct
yourself with a little more dignity.

239
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,588
I'm talking to you, stupid!

240
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:46,388
Why don't you take your
own advice for once?

241
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:47,930
But look!

242
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,631
He dodged that kick without even blinking!

243
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,740
In fact, he even looks happy!

244
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,160
I thought he was gonna die!

245
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,797
Stop making that damn face!

246
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,586
Don't do the same joke twice!

247
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:07,580
I've had enough.

248
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,600
Like I said, this guy is mine.

249
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,580
You go ahead.

250
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,881
I'll catch up with you two later.

251
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:23,122
So you're saying the rear
two cars were detached?

252
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:25,997
How could you allow something
like this to happen?

253
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,637
My deepest apologies, ma 'am.

254
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:30,917
But in our defense, even Captain T-Bone
got trapped in one of those cars,

255
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,677
and you know how powerful he is.

256
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:33,590
Fine.

257
00:14:33,673 --> 00:14:35,877
Give me a status report on
what's left of the train.

258
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:36,790
Yes, ma 'am.

259
00:14:36,873 --> 00:14:40,597
As of now, in addition to the engine
room, there are five cars still with us.

260
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:43,917
All of the military in the
fifth car have been taken out.

261
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,740
That leaves Wanze guarding the fourth car?

262
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,145
Nero on duty in the third car!

263
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,704
Nico Robin up in the first car?

264
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,218
and everyone here in the second car.

265
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:58,060
It seems our enemy is
not to be taken lightly.

266
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:00,777
However, the only
problem that concerns me?

267
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,017
In our current situation.

268
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:05,041
is that Franky is walking
around this train free.

269
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:08,577
Our mission was to take
Franky and Nico Robin into

270
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:11,677
custody and then deliver
them securely to Eni's lobby.

271
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,525
As long as we accomplish that,

272
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:17,457
I don't care how many men we lose
or how we take care of our enemies.

273
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,599
That has no bearing on our mission.

274
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:23,860
And were you able to
identify the intruders? Yes.

275
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:26,357
First there were the two
men that we had in custody,

276
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:29,897
but now it seems one of those two is
wearing some sort of strange mask.

277
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:32,737
There's also a blonde guy in a
suit that we've never seen before,

278
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:34,820
making a total of three intruders.

279
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:40,277
He's probably a member of the Straw Hat
Pirates just like that long-nosed man is.

280
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:43,536
Naturally, their purpose
here is to rescue Nico Robin.

281
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:47,507
And, since they freed him,
Frankie's decided to help them out.

282
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:52,422
Hey, Looch, would you like me to
go and keep an eye on Nico Robin?

283
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:53,775
That's not necessary.

284
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,397
Just stay focused on recapturing Franky.

285
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,117
Nothing else matters to him.

286
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:01,860
So, they want to take
Nico Robin back, do they?

287
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:03,749
Sorry to break it to them.

288
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,717
But that's just not gonna happen.

289
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:10,100
I won't let you pass!

290
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,380
Letting the heck out of the floor!

291
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:18,746
Is he gonna bring out
the ramen noodles again?

292
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,300
Ramen beans!

293
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,480
This is sharp!

294
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:31,980
Damn it!

295
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:43,257
Let's head over on the roof.

296
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:44,170
Right.

297
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,677
We'll leave it to you then, Sanji.

298
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:47,590
Best of luck.

299
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,600
Go, go, go, go!

300
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:52,800
They're go, go, go gone!

301
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:55,500
But I suppose that's no big deal.

302
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,757
Because the person waiting
for them in the next car?

303
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,800
is one tough customer, Nero!

304
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,593
He's the latest addition to
CP9, an assassin for justice.

305
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:04,877
Those two are dead meat.

306
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:07,997
If there's one thing that
Nero loves to do, it's kill.

307
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,160
Go, go, go, go!

308
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,660
Ah, flinchy.

309
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:14,810
Shoot!

310
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,420
I told you, I'm in a hurry here.

311
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,580
Okay then, fine.

312
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:25,020
Ramen Kenpo Noodle Slicer!

313
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,080
Let's see how you like this!

314
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,940
Fire escape lane!

315
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:49,540
Not only did you disrespect my beautiful
attack, you kicked me ten times,

316
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,630
didn't you?

317
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:53,145
Actually, it was twelve times.

318
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:54,560
Hey, you!

319
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:57,360
Are you secretly super
strong or something?

320
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:59,157
It's not really a secret.

321
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,946
Maybe you're just super weak.

322
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:02,160
Super weak!

323
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,397
Not even my old man would say
something like that to me!

324
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,310
How dare you!

325
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,340
I'm Woods!

326
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,715
I wouldn't let you get away with this!

327
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:10,830
Rude!

328
00:18:10,913 --> 00:18:13,377
Besides, I was simply distracted
by your swirling eyebrows.

329
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,517
They make me dizzy.

330
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,057
That's why I fell for your attack.

331
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,277
Still, you're a good fighter.

332
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:18,517
Too bad you look weird.

333
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:19,457
Hey, you freak!

334
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:22,540
You're in no position to
call anyone weird looking!

335
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:27,037
After that failed attack,

336
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:30,977
I feel like I need to prove myself, so
I'm gonna show you something amazing!

337
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:34,060
This is why I was chosen
to escort those criminals!

338
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:47,680
Ramen Kimpo, secret technique!

339
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,497
Ramen Kimpo, secret technique!

340
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:56,800
Uh, what the hell is all that?

341
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:59,920
It's my incredible edible combat uniform!

342
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:05,560
Ramen's polo suit!

343
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,240
Now fight!

344
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:08,680
Go, go, go, go!

345
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:11,877
The secret of this
ramen kenpo technique is

346
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,597
controlling the three
moving noodles at will!

347
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:15,510
See?

348
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,360
Bastard, how dare you disgrace
food like that, you weirdo!

349
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:23,480
My speed, my power, and
my special abilities!

350
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:27,220
I'm at a different level now
in all those areas! Yeah!

351
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:32,500
If showing you isn't enough,
I'm gonna boot it into you! Go!

352
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,940
Just shut up already and get on with it.

353
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:43,242
But prepare yourself, cause I'm gonna make
you eat every last one of those noodles.

354
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:49,210
Question.

355
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,180
Who are you?

356
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,968
What are you doing up here?

357
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,880
The officer in charge of the third car,

358
00:19:58,080 --> 00:20:01,160
a four powers master,
and a new recruit in CP9,

359
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,120
the sea weasel, Nero.

360
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:10,020
Unfortunately, I'm under
specific orders not to kill you.

361
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:14,585
You know, you being one of our
most important criminals and all.

362
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,560
All right, that's one half.

363
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:19,637
Now tell me what you're doing up
here on the roof of this train.

364
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,217
If you'd just waited inside,
I would have come to you.

365
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,377
Well, how was I supposed to know that?

366
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:27,813
You may have tried to cheat
and skip right past this car.

367
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,940
My, my, my.

368
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:31,737
That's rather cautious of you.

369
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:35,857
But in your line of work, you always
got to keep your guard up, right?

370
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:39,528
By the way, what's that
weird-looking thing there behind you?

371
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:40,850
Huh?

372
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:50,620
That was a dirty trick.

373
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,760
Of course it was!

374
00:20:56,140 --> 00:21:00,140
They don't call me the King of Water
Seven's underworld for nothing.

375
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:05,240
Don't go down, Octoshoes.

376
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:24,300
Who knows, is that you?

377
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,480
Why are you here?
